# Planning notes live in docs/plans

Before any non-trivial code or config change:

1. Write (or update) a planning note under **`docs/plans/`**.
2. Name files `YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.md` (UTC or local project date).
3. Keep the same content in the chat reply (summary OK if the file is complete).
4. Link new plans from `docs/plans/README.md` when adding a plan.
5. Do **not** implement until the user approves the plan (unless they already said approve implement).

## Required plan sections

- What / why
- Architectural impact (vs `docs/architecture.md`)
- Risks + mitigations
- Doc updates required
- Test plan
- Implementation order

## Exceptions

- Typo-only / one-line comment fixes: no plan file required.
- Pure chat Q&A with no repo edits: no plan file.
